    "blocky-image-with-text-4007e7c5": {
      "type": "blocky-image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "title_WeGmfK": {
          "type": "title",
          "settings": {
            "title": "<strong>Where To Set It So The Rain Plays It</strong>",
            "title_size": 40,
            "title_color": "#000000"
          }
        },
        "body_VhUrpx": {
          "type": "body",
          "settings": {
            "body_text": "<p>\"A soft drizzle is too light to ring steel. You want the big drops,\" Evelyn says.</p><p>Set it where rain gathers and falls: under the drip edge of your porch roof, below a gutter, or beneath a branch that keeps dripping after a storm. Tilt it a little so the water runs off.</p><p>In a steady rain, every drop lands on a note. On dry days, pick up the mallet and play it yourself.</p>",
            "body_size": 18,
            "body_color": "#000000"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
